        "id": "how-do-we-put-the-cayman-holding-company-in-place-before-a-listing",
        "question": "How do we put the Cayman holding company in place before a listing?",
        "answerHtml": "<p>The usual path is a share exchange: the Cayman exempted company is incorporated, and the existing shareholders of the operating company swap their shares for shares of the new Cayman parent, mirroring the old cap table at the top of the new structure. Cayman counsel then conforms the memorandum and articles of association to what the SEC, the exchange, and any depositary bank require — share classes, transfer mechanics, board provisions — and delivers the legal opinions the process demands. Tax analysis in every relevant jurisdiction belongs at the start, not the end, since the exchange itself can have consequences for shareholders in some countries. Done early, the restructuring is routine; done late, it compresses the <a href=\"/products/nasdaq-direct-listing\">F-1</a> calendar. We coordinate the Cayman workstream alongside the audit so neither waits on the other.</p><p><em>Related topics:</em> <a href=\"/products/nasdaq-direct-listing\">NASDAQ Direct Listing</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products/nyse-direct-listing\">NYSE Direct Listing</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products/reg-s\">Regulation S</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products\">Our Product Line</a></p>",
