        "id": "how-quickly-can-the-company-be-formed-and-what-does-it-take-to-maintai",
        "question": "How quickly can the company be formed, and what does it take to maintain?",
        "answerHtml": "<p>Formation is fast: a Cayman exempted company can be incorporated in 1–4 business days, with same-day express service available. There is no minimum share capital, share classes can be structured freely — including the dual-class arrangements founders often want going into a <a href=\"/products/nyse-direct-listing\">listing</a> — and 100% foreign ownership is permitted with no local director requirement. The company must maintain a registered office in the islands through a licensed local agent, keep its registers (including the beneficial-ownership register, which is not public), file an annual return, and pay annual government fees; typical all-in maintenance runs about $5,000–9,500 a year depending on authorized capital. Board meetings can be held anywhere, and no annual general meeting need take place in the territory. For a pure holding company above an operating group, the economic-substance requirements are generally light — a point we confirm with Cayman counsel case by case.</p><p><em>Related topics:</em> <a href=\"/products/nasdaq-direct-listing\">NASDAQ Direct Listing</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products/nyse-direct-listing\">NYSE Direct Listing</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products/reg-s\">Regulation S</a> &middot; <a href=\"/products\">Our Product Line</a></p>",
